WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.320
At harvest time, the Torah tells farmers
not to reap the corners of their fields.

2
00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:09.100
Whatever grows there is left
for the poor and the stranger.

3
00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:13.340
Today, the Hebrew word for
giving to the poor is tzedakah.

4
00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:16.430
It comes from tzedek,
the word for justice.

5
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.420
So why call giving justice,
and not simply charity?

6
00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.400
In this mission, you'll climb a famous
ladder with eight levels of giving,

7
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.390
from lowest to highest.

8
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.650
Then you'll meet acts of loving-kindness,

9
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:32.690
and the Jewish idea of healing,
or repairing, the world.

10
00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:37.960
Your mission: find out why Jews call
giving to the poor justice, not charity.
